desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Insecure Resteasy Deserialization"
	title_zh: "Insecure Resteasy Deserialization"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-insecure-resteasy-deserialization"
	risk: "deserialization"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
When a Restful webservice endpoint is configured to use wildcard mediaType {*/*} as a value for the @Consumes annotation, an attacker could abuse the SerializableProvider by sending a HTTP Request with a Content-Type of application/x-java-serialized-object. The body of that request would be processed by the SerializationProvider and could contain a malicious payload, which may lead to arbitrary code execution when calling the $Y.getObject method.

### 风险类型
不安全反序列化（deserialization）

### 影响
反序列化不可信数据可能触发任意代码执行或对象注入。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.

### 参考
- CWE: CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
避免反序列化不可信输入，使用安全的数据格式，并校验数据来源与类型。
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.java": <<<POS
@Consumes({"application/x-java-serialized-object"})
POS
	"safefile://pos.java": <<<NEG
@Consumes({"application/json"})
NEG
)

${*.java}.pattern_regex(/(?:@Consumes\(\{"application\/x\-java\-serialized\-object"\}\))|(?:@Consumes\(\{"\*\/\*"\}\))|(?:@Consumes\("\*\/\*"\))|(?:@Consumes\(\{MediaType\.WILDCARD_TYPE\}\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Insecure Resteasy Deserialization",
	title_zh: "Insecure Resteasy Deserialization",
	message: "Insecure Resteasy Deserialization detected.",
}
